From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 10:34:12 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: advertise
 VK_EXT_external_memory_acquire_unmodified

VP_ANDROID_17_requirements makes this extension mandatory. It depends
only on VK_KHR_external_memory, which this driver already advertises, and
it defines no features and no commands: it only lets an application chain
VkExternalMemoryAcquireUnmodifiedEXT onto a buffer or image memory
barrier to say that a foreign or external queue left the contents alone
while it owned them.

The structure is a hint. An implementation is free to ignore it and
perform the ordinary acquire, which is what happens here, so the contents
stay correct either way. Metal's unified memory gives the acquire nothing
to invalidate, and there is no cheaper path to select. The renderer and
the guest Venus driver already pass the extension through, so the host
driver was the only layer withholding it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
index f1b60389d7e004b57ccba4239532a6237ab04a8c..5fdcf54b2a2c3e1c0b9a97a8a72eb6ca5f1ca5db 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_physical_device.c
@@ -174,6 +174,7 @@ kk_get_device_extensions(const struct kk_instance *instance,
       .EXT_depth_clip_enable = true,
       .EXT_dynamic_rendering_unused_attachments = true,
       .EXT_extended_dynamic_state3 = true,
+      .EXT_external_memory_acquire_unmodified = true,
       .EXT_external_memory_metal = true,
       .EXT_graphics_pipeline_library = true,
       .EXT_external_memory_host = true,
